  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the claim direction. For SMARCA4-loss claims with direction -1, a positive signed estimate means a lower raw dependency_composite in SMARCA4-loss versus intact, i.e. stronger composite dependency. For TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss claims with direction +1, a positive signed estimate means a higher raw dependency_composite, i.e. weaker composite dependency. H67 shows that SMARCA4-loss in adenocarcinoma is associated with lower composite dependency (+0.778 [0.701, 0.854]), far above the 0.15-unit threshold; H95 confirms this in a TP53/KEAP1-intact adenocarcinoma background (+0.796 [0.743, 0.848]). H96 confirms a similarly large squamous effect in the same cleaner background (+0.861 [0.770, 0.953]). Thus the adenocarcinoma main effect and the squamous main effect are both robust and scientifically meaningful. H97, however, is only +0.065 [-0.040, 0.170], with a point estimate well below threshold and an interval spanning zero; it does not support meaningful lineage modification in this simpler background. I reject H97 and close it. This makes the unrestricted reversed lineage interaction H94 much less compelling: its point estimate (+0.211 [0.063, 0.359]) remains above threshold but its lower bound does not, and the cleaner background result suggests it may reflect co-loss composition or residual confounding rather than a robust lineage-specific modification. I keep H94 unresolved but defer further investigation rather than pursuing it as a priority. H69 and H98 show that KEAP1-loss is associated with higher dependency_composite in adenocarcinoma overall (+0.814 [0.734, 0.894]) and in a TP53/SMARCA4-intact adenocarcinoma background (+0.768 [0.706, 0.829]), and H100 rejects lineage modification for KEAP1-loss in that cleaner background (-0.053 [-0.151, 0.045]). The co-loss conditional main effects also persist: TP53-loss within KEAP1-loss is +0.576 [0.414, 0.739], SMARCA4-loss within KEAP1-loss is +0.809 [0.678, 0.940], and KEAP1-loss within SMARCA4-loss is +0.845 [0.714, 0.976]. These are descriptive subgroup associations, not causal interaction estimates; conditioning on co-losses can introduce selection structure and does not adjust for all correlated features. The key unresolved context interaction remains H31, TP53-by-KEAP1, with discovery point estimate +0.210 but lower bound +0.019. Because the point exceeds threshold but the interval does not clear threshold, and because many interactions have been tested, I request independent validation for H31 rather than accepting or rejecting it now. Non-Avana library robustness checks are large and internally sufficient: H104 is +0.870 [0.737, 1.003] and H105 is +0.979 [0.792, 1.167]. Their exposed cell sizes are modest, but lower bounds exceed the threshold and directions match the validated global associations, so I accept them as dataset-supported robustness checks and do not request validation on them. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal knockout effects, mechanistic pathway claims, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Core dataset-supported associations remain: TP53-loss with higher dependency_composite/weaker composite dependency, SMARCA4-loss with lower dependency_composite/stronger composite dependency, and KEAP1-loss with higher dependency_composite/weaker composite dependency. New lineage analyses accept SMARCA4-loss adenocarcinoma main effects (H67 unrestricted, H95 TP53/KEAP1-intact) and squamous TP53/KEAP1-intact effect H96, while rejecting meaningful lineage interaction in the cleaner background H97. KEAP1-loss adenocarcinoma effects are similarly robust overall H69 and in TP53/SMARCA4-intact background H98; lineage interaction H100 is null. The unrestricted reversed SMARCA4 lineage interaction H94 remains not accepted and is deferred because the cleaner-background null H97 suggests the apparent overall interaction may be confounded by co-loss distribution. Co-loss conditional main effects are accepted and closed: TP53-loss within KEAP1-loss H101, SMARCA4-loss within KEAP1-loss H102, and KEAP1-loss within SMARCA4-loss H103. These do not by themselves prove interaction; they are descriptive stratum associations and conditioning can introduce selection structure. The key unresolved context interaction is H31 TP53-by-KEAP1: discovery +0.210 [0.019, 0.400], point above threshold but lower bound below threshold, with multiple-interaction multiplicity concern. Validation requested for H31. Non-Avana library checks are accepted: SMARCA4-loss H104 and KEAP1-loss H105 are both large with lower bounds above threshold, though cell sizes are modest. Guardrails: composite endpoint only, no causality or external generalizability, independent validation indicates internal robustness not mechanism. Next: assess H31 validation; if interval clears threshold, accept TP53/KEAP1 context modification; otherwise close. Lower-priority residual technical checks include high-Cas9 KEAP1 H72, screen-quality interactions H75/H76, screen_nnmd main effects H85/H86, and TP53 screen-quality H36/H37.",
